That project is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. These things
are taken from it. src/codes.rs holds the published code lists its linters
check against — countries, currencies, freight unit types — decoded from the
bitfields it stores them as into sorted arrays. data/reference-vectors.txt
holds the UNIT_TEST_PASS and UNIT_TEST_FAIL cases from its lint_*.c files,
extracted verbatim, which tests/reference.rs runs against this crate's own
checks. data/digital-link-vectors.txt holds the test_URIescape and
test_URIunescape cases from its dl.c, likewise extracted verbatim, which
tests/digital_link.rs runs against this crate's percent-encoding. src/coupon.rs
is translated from its lint_couponcode.c and lint_couponposoffer.c, and the
percent-encoding in src/digital_link.rs from the URIescape and URIunescape
functions of its dl.c; both are modified, and say so in their module
documentation. The other modules implement the same published rules —
the General Specifications and the Digital Link Standard — in their own way,
and do not reproduce its code.
